person.about_me:
How can I help?

If you are looking for pragmatic, practical business advice relating to:

•	Mergers and acquisitions;
•	IPOs and secondary issues on Aquis (formerly NEX), AIM or the Official List;
•	Public takeovers;
•	Restructurings;
•	Corporate governance;
•	Joint Ventures;
•	Partnerships and LLPs; and
•	Private equity and other investments.

I deal with all sizes of companies from start-ups and SMEs to multi nationals.  I have not just advised clients over the last 25 years but also negotiated Shakespeare Martineau's mergers, sat on the Members Board (dealing with partner issues and remuneration) and acted as non executive on our Main Board.  This has given me additional insight into running a business and dealing with issues.

‘Keith Spedding is a top-notch lawyer who never fails to deliver on M&A and related transactions.’
Legal500 2024 testimonial

If you want more information or to see if I can help then please contact me.

Working in the insurance industry for 36 years specialising in mid-market UK Corporate and Commercial Placements. Responsible for managing the London Retail Division and looking to grow our footprint in the Southern Region. Continue to manage the relationships of some of our key clients ranging from Housing Associations, Construction, Tech and Manufacturing. Enjoy talking to people (after 10am!) and problem solving.  

Hobbies/Interest - Massive foodie and take my football very seriously.  Relax watching cooking programmes, TV shows and movies (whilst drinking wine!)

Interesting Fact – Fear of Clowns (including Mime Artists!), the feeling of wanting to throw myself off at heights, hate coriander and karaoke!

