25 years’ experience in commodities and financial services, primarily as a COO / business manager delivering change and managing all aspects of the front-to-back development and support of the business.  Previous employment includes
-	global business manager for J.P. Morgan’s Global Clearing business, covering futures & options, OTC and securities clearing;
-	business manager for European power & gas and dry bulk commodities at Deutsche Bank;
-	various roles at UBS Investment Bank, starting from their graduate training programme, through operations, technology and business management roles in the Exchange Traded Derivatives business, to COO for the Commodities business in Europe & Asia Pacific.

Richard is head of Winckworth Sherwood's Corporate, Banking and Finance team. He advises registered providers, property developers, house builders, public sector clients, SME's, high net worth clients and entrepreneurs on:

- governance issues and corporate structures;
- real estate joint ventures, and corporate acquisitions and disposals of land;
- strategic alliances, partnerships and shareholders' agreements;
- procurement, outsourcing and commercial agreements (including business transfers).

Recent projects include:
• advising G15 registered providers on good governance, matters of vires, interpretation of and changes to their Rules, corporate structures and acquisitions and mergers;

• advising various leading developers on acquisition structures and joint ventures with Transport for London, Hyde Housing, MSREF, CPC Group, British Land, L&Q and various local authorities;

• assisting various G15 registered providers on corporate structures and joint venture arrangements with Mount Anvil, Countryside, Galliford Try, Berkeley, Hill, Bellway, Crest Nicholson, Nicholas King Homes, London Square and various local authorities;

• supporting developers and fund managers on the acquisition and disposal of real estate assets via corporate vehicles.

• helping a family office with the creation and ongoing maintenance of corporate entities for the purposes of owning and operating multiple aircraft;

• advising on the procurement, commercial and corporate aspects of a project established to create a new national certification body, serviced by supply arrangements concluded via competitive tender;

• advising a company on various software development contracts and related arrangements for implementation of a national IT system, including migration from legacy systems.

Experienced and personable CFO (Chartered Accountant) and MD

Key skills:
•	Managing and influencing internal and external stakeholders including shareholders, partners, banks, franchise partners, solicitors, auditors and tax advisers, insurers, H&S and HR advisers, valuers, landlords, and wealth managers;
•	Leadership of on-site management and head office shared services, including finance, HR, marketing, sales, revenue and IT;
•	Fundraising (debt and equity);
•	Acquisition analysis, execution and post-acquisition integration;
•	Dealing with complex and evolving group structures;
•	Legal document analysis and negotiation;
•	Profitability forecasting, pro-active results and issues monitoring, working capital control and reactive analysis of financials;
•	Internal process re-design, improvement and monitoring – both financial and non-financial, through periods of rapid growth; 
•	Leading all tax analysis, including Corporation Tax, VAT, capital allowances, personal tax, BPRA, EIS.

•	Experienced Chief Financial Officer and Chartered Accountant;
•	Contributed as CFO/FD to the profitable growth of mid-market businesses;
•	Achievements in transforming/scaling up financial processes, discipline, reporting and structure to support a high growth environment;
•	Key business leader in a range of activities and transactions including raising funding, business sale (including private equity), business acquisition and integration, restructuring, start-up and development/implementation of business strategy; 
•	Extensive International experience, notably US, gained in a range of businesses.
•	Experience in complex international Engineering/Manufacturing/Technology businesses;
•	Motivational leader, skilled at encouraging and empowering staff resulting in a high performing fully  engaged workforce.

